             * base URL, TIN, id type and id value, keyed with a sub-key
             * derived from the application key.
             *
             * WHY KEYED, AND NOT A PLAIN HASH. A Malaysian business
             * registration number is twelve digits. An NRIC is twelve digits
             * whose first six are a date of birth and whose middle two are a
             * state code, so the real search space is under 10^8. A bare
             * sha256 of either is exhausted on a laptop in well under a
             * second -- anyone who obtained this table would obtain the
             * identifiers. Keying it means a stolen backup, a misconfigured
             * replica or a careless SELECT is not enough on its own.
